WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.240
- Huh. Adnan Syed from
the "Serial" podcast

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.520
was released from jail.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.513
No, that's way too controversial for me.

00:00:07.513 --> 00:00:09.679
(bright music)

00:00:09.679 --> 00:00:10.737
(phone rings)

00:00:10.737 --> 00:00:12.570
- Hello?
- Hey buddy.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:14.610
- Thanks Devin, and I mean that.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:18.180
Thank you for having me
be the sacrificial lamb

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.090
talking about a wildly
controversial subject

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.710
that will almost certainly result

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.690
in irrational attacks on me.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.160
I'm doubling my fee, Devin.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.960
Check the invoice.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.410
Adnan Syed, the subject of
the most popular podcast

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.610
of all time,

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.540
is a free man.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.160
- The stunning reversal in a case

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.380
that inspired the "Serial" podcast.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.480
- Officials have dropped all
charges against Adnan Syed

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.610
after he spent 23 years in prison.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.830
- [Reporter] Adnan Syed is a free man.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.158
- He walked out of a
Baltimore courthouse today.

00:00:46.158 --> 00:00:49.950
- Syed was convicted of
murdering Hae Min Lee in 1999.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.440
This doesn't mean that
he's necessarily innocent,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.990
but the State's Attorney for
Baltimore, Marilyn Mosby,

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.480
has just announced that
the state is dropping

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.370
all charges against Syed.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.160
- This morning, I instructed my office

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.270
to dismiss the criminal
case against Adnan Syed

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:09.180
following the completion of a second round

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:11.910
of touch DNA testing

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.517
of items that were never tested before.

00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:16.530
- Adnan Syed's case was featured

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.690
on the first season of
the podcast "Serial"

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:21.090
which became a true crime sensation.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.967
The podcast was downloaded
over 100 million times.

00:01:24.967 --> 00:01:27.840
"Serial" inspired other
podcasts about the case,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.930
several documentaries and
multiple criminal appeals

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:32.280
of Syed's sentence.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.400
This case is also
incredibly controversial,

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:39.030
with some people convinced that
Syed is absolutely innocent.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.740
- I'm innocent, right?

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.450
Just like everybody else here.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.160
- And others equally convinced

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.020
that he's an unrepentant murderer.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.310
- You guys are pathetic.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.690
You're idolizing a murderer.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.340
- In this episode we're gonna explain

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.600
how we got to the point

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.390
of Syed walking free after 23 years,

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.970
but we are not gonna
try and solve the case.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:59.010
In other words, we're
doing the characteristic

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.720
Legal Eagle thing,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.050
which is annoy everyone
who has a strong opinion.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.670
It's the Legal Eagle brand.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.310
Let's go back to 1999.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:10.290
In 1999, Hae Min Lee was an honor student

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.990
at Woodlawn High School in
Baltimore County, Maryland.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.580
On January 23rd of that year,

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.900
when she was 18 years old,

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.940
Lee disappeared after leaving school.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.040
There were no witnesses
to her disappearance.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:20.910
One month later,

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:22.650
her body was found at Leakin Park.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:24.870
Police determined that she
had been strangled to death

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.120
and they eventually arrested Adnan Syed,

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.190
Lee's 17-year-old ex-boyfriend,

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:30.450
and charged him with murder.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.220
Syed was also an honor student,

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.120
but during the trial

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.100
prosecutors made hundreds of references

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.960
to Adnan's race and religion,

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.827
introducing him to the jury by saying,

00:02:38.827 --> 00:02:42.120
"The defendant is of Pakistani
background, he's a Muslim."

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.130
Now this was used to explain

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:46.350
the religious and familial tensions

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.540
that ultimately led to the breakup

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.040
between Lee and Syed

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.750
and hence a motive to kill.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.753
But it's not a great look.

00:02:53.753 --> 00:02:56.500
- What we've got here is

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.510
failure to communicate.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:00.630
- At the time of trial,

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:03.810
there was no DNA evidence
linking Syed to the murder.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.790
Instead, the state relayed mostly

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.740
on the testimony of Jay Wilds,

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.930
a friend of Syed's who
was a known drug dealer.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:12.030
Wilds was a year older than Lee and Syed

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.620
and had graduated the year before.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.320
He eventually told the
police that Syed killed Lee.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.300
Wilds allegedly drove to the park

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.546
where he watched Syed bury Lee's body.

00:03:20.546 --> 00:03:22.530
Here's the basic version of events

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.930
the prosecution presented
during the trial.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.210
Around lunchtime on the
day Lee disappeared,

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:30.360
Syed tells Wilds that
he's going to kill Lee.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.940
Wilds then borrows
Syed's car and cellphone

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:36.360
on the condition that Wilds
drops Syed off at school,

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.193
which he does.

00:03:37.193 --> 00:03:39.990
Wilds then goes to his
friend Jenn Pusateri's house

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:40.823
to hang out.

00:03:40.823 --> 00:03:42.030
Syed has a free period

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:44.100
and then gets to his psychology class late

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.930
at 1:27 p.m.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:50.220
That class ends at 2:15
p.m. and, according to Syed,

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.930
he goes to track practice later

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.930
from 3:30 to 4:30 or 5:00.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:55.980
Up to this point,

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:00.000
the timelines from Syed and
Wilds are largely similar,

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.970
but this is also where they
start to diverge substantially.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.710
And it's this gap in time,

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.960
2:15 to 3:30,

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.850
that the prosecution focuses on

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:11.250
as the time Syed kills Lee.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.420
According to Wilds,

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.850
Syed calls him at some
point in the afternoon

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:16.980
asking Wilds to pick him up later.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.050
Not hearing anything further from Syed,

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.300
Wilds eventually leaves Pusateri's house

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.340
and drives to his friend Jeff's house.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:24.420
Jeff wasn't home

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.700
and as Wilds is leaving the neighborhood

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.230
he gets a call from Syed

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.180
asking him to meet at Best Buy.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.940
It's notable that Wilds believed this call

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.530
was around 3:30 or so.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:35.970
Both he and Pusateri

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:38.940
remember Wilds leaving
her house around 3:30.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:41.310
But the prosecution used a cellphone log

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:44.130
to argue that this phone
call from Syed to Wilds

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.560
actually happened at 2:36.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:48.870
Remember, it is important
to the prosecution

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:53.250
that the murder happened some
time between 2:15 and 3:30.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.180
According to Wilds,

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.460
he meets Syed at the Best Buy parking lot

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.440
where Syed shows him Lee's body

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.820
in the trunk of her own car.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.880
They then ditch Lee's car
at the I-70 Park and Ride

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.290
and after buying some marijuana

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:07.020
Wilds drops Syed off at track practice.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:09.960
Wilds later picks Syed
up from track practice,

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:11.910
Syed retrieves Lee's car,

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.610
and ultimately they end up at Leakin Park.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:16.170
Wilds also testifies

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.660
that Syed's phone received two phone calls

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:21.060
while Syed was digging a
hole through Lee's body.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:24.390
The cellphone records showed
two incoming phone calls

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.640
at 7:09 and 7:16

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.410
on the day Lee disappeared.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:31.680
The state then called an
expert from AT&amp;T who testified

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.380
that the cell towers where
the calls were received

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:37.560
were connected with cell
sites around Leakin Park.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.680
Wilds' version of events was
somehow backed up by Pusateri.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:43.050
She confirms that Wilds was at her house

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.820
until about 3:30.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.370
She also told police that
when she tried to call Wilds

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:48.990
on Syed's phone that day,

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.960
someone else answered and
told her Wilds was busy.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:54.270
She also said that Wilds later told her

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:56.610
he saw Lee's body at the Best Buy

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.170
and that Syed strangled Lee

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.450
because Lee broke Syed's heart.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:02.550
Now something is worth
saying at this point.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:03.840
This has been a quick summary

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.450
and it's not intended to
capture all the issues

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:09.000
identified by people
scrutinizing this case.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:09.840
Fans of "Serial"

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.760
are probably tearing
their hair out right now.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.970
- I'm mad as hell, I'm
not gonna take it anymore!

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:15.870
- For one thing,

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.990
the version of events
Wilds testified to at trial

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:22.080
was similar to but not
altogether consistent

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.360
with his two interviews with police.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:26.970
Wilds himself later told an
interviewer from The Intercept

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.920
that he was terrified of going to prison

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.930
for dealing marijuana
to high school students

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:32.040
and he was also afraid

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.750
it would somehow implicate his family

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.340
since he based his operations

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:36.990
out of his grandmother's house.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:38.820
Originally, Pusateri told police

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:41.190
that she didn't know
anything about what happened.

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:43.080
Years later, Pusateri would say

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.487
that Wilds was always very convincing.

00:06:45.487 --> 00:06:46.890
"He was a good storyteller.

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:48.900
He would make you believe
your shirt was green

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.130
if it was blue."

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.830
When confronted with the many
versions of Wilds' story,

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:54.870
including one where he sees Lee's body

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:57.480
behind some rowhouses
rather than the Best Buy,

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:00.540
Pusateri concluded that "Jay
obviously picks and chooses

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:01.373
what he tells,

00:07:01.373 --> 00:07:04.140
and at this point, it's
created such a mess."

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:06.030
Wilds agreed to cooperate with the police

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:09.030
and was actually charged as
an accessory after the fact.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.610
He told the jury that the
crime was premeditated,

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:13.117
that he heard Syed saying,

00:07:13.117 --> 00:07:14.910
"I'm going to kill that bitch,"

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.040
just hours before she disappeared.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:20.220
He also testified that Syed
bragged about the murder

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:22.267
when he showed Wilds the body, saying,

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:25.260
"I killed someone with my bare hands."

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:26.430
Syed's defense was

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:28.620
that he couldn't have
committed the murder.

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:30.810
He went to school, he
went to track practice,

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.490
and then he went to pray at his mosque

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.350
with his father for Ramadan.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:35.310
Needless to say,

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:38.850
a jury found him guilty of
murder, robbery, kidnapping,

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:39.990
and false imprisonment,

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.850
and he was sentenced to life in prison.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:44.580
The "Serial" podcast
presented a new witness,

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.204
a woman who allegedly
saw Syed at the library

00:07:47.204 --> 00:07:49.650
between 2:30 and 2:40

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:51.360
on the day Lee went missing.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.280
Remember, the prosecution argued

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:55.050
that the murder had to have happened

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:57.870
between 2:15 and 3:30 or so.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.370
The witness, Asia McClain,

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.980
said that she tried to
testify at Syed's trial

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.990
but that his lawyer, Maria Gutierrez,

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:05.340
never contacted her.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:09.030
It's notable that Gutierrez
was disbarred in 2001

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:11.160
after a series of client complaints.

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.530
The podcast also
questioned the reliability

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:15.210
of the cellphone tower records

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:18.300
and revealed that physical
evidence gathered in 1999

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:21.360
was never tested for Mr. Syed's DNA.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:23.580
In 2015, momentum from "Serial"

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:26.400
helped Syed file an
appeal with new lawyers.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.740
A state court granted Syed a new trial

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:29.970
after his lawyers showed

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:32.550
that Gutierrez had been grossly negligent

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:35.220
for not calling McClain
as an alibi witness.

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:36.570
The lawyers also questioned

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.000
the reliability of the
cell tower evidence.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.730
Now Gutierrez had died in 2007,

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:43.800
so she was unable to testify

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.500
about why she didn't investigate McClain.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:49.650
In 2018, the Maryland
Court of Special Appeals

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:52.410
upheld the decision to
grant Syed a new trial

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:53.880
and vacated his conviction

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.290
on the grounds that he received

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.120
inadequate legal assistance.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:57.953
- Now didn't I tell you

00:08:57.953 --> 00:08:59.310
the next time you appear in my courtroom

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:01.053
that you dress appropriately?

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:05.100
- You was serious about that?

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.440
- The state then appealed
to Marylan's highest court,

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:08.970
the Court of Appeals.

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:10.230
Let's take a step back.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:13.740
What did Adnan Syed have to
prove to get a new trial?

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.900
Syed's legal team raised a claim called

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:17.520
ineffective assistance of counsel

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.170
in violation of the Sixth Amendment

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:20.670
of the United States Constitution.

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:23.640
Syed's defense team presented
one issue on appeal,

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:26.010
that he was denied effective
assistance of counsel

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:28.980
because Gutierrez failed to even interview

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:30.390
the alibi witness.

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:32.700
An alibi witness is a defendant's claim

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:35.130
that he or she was at another place

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.620
at the time where the
alleged crime was committed.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:38.910
In Strickland v. Washington,

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:42.000
the US Supreme Court
outlined a two-pronged test

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.160
for determining whether
a criminal defendant

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.650
has received ineffective
assistance of counsel.

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:48.240
The defendant must first prove

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:50.880
that the trial counsel's
performance was deficient.

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:52.920
If the lawyer's performance was deficient,

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:54.240
then the defendant has to prove

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.160
that he suffered actual prejudice

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:57.990
by trial counsel's deficiency.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:00.240
In other words, the
defendant has to demonstrate

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:03.030
that if not for his
counsel's bad performance,

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:05.190
there was a substantial probability

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:08.040
that the jury would not have
convicted the defendant.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.830
The Maryland Court of
Appeals ruled against Syed

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:12.120
in a four-to-three decision

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:14.370
that overturned the lower court ruling.

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:16.110
The Court of Appeals first held

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:18.120
that under the deficient-performance prong

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:19.470
of Strickland v. Washington,

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:20.550
at a minimum,

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.890
Syed's trial counsel had a duty

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.260
to contact the potential alibi witness

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:28.110
to investigate or explore
that person's background

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:30.480
as a potential as an alibi witness.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:31.980
The American Bar Association's

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.480
standard for defense counsel

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:36.690
required them to conduct
a prompt investigation

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.370
of the circumstances of the case

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.980
and explore all avenues leading to facts

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:42.810
relevant to the merits of the case

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:45.210
and the penalty in the
event of conviction.

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:46.890
The investigation should include

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:48.750
efforts to secure information

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.400
in the possession of the prosecution

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.410
and law enforcement authorities.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:55.560
Gutierrez's failure to
contact an alibi witness

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:57.540
constituted deficient performance

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.970
under the first prong
of the Strickland test.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.830
The second prong of the Strickland test

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:04.440
asks whether trial counsel's
deficient performance

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:05.820
resulted in prejudice.

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:06.930
To show prejudice,

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:08.430
a defendant has to show

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.410
that there is a reasonable probability

00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:13.410
that but for a counsel's
unprofessional errors,

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:16.024
the result of the proceeding
would have been different.

00:11:16.024 --> 00:11:17.460
Under this standard,

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.440
a defendant must demonstrate either, one,

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:20.850
a reasonable probability

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:23.730
that but for counsel's
unprofessional errors

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:25.950
the result of the proceeding
would have been different,

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.230
or two, that the result of the proceeding

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:31.650
was fundamentally unfair or unreliable.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:33.450
The key question in this analysis

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:36.420
is what constitutes
reasonable probability.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.077
The Supreme Court described it as

00:11:38.077 --> 00:11:41.130
"a probability sufficient
to undermine confidence

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.360
in the outcome."

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:45.150
Maryland courts interpret
reasonable probability to mean

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:48.480
that "there was a substantial
or significant possibility

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:50.550
that the verdict of the trier of fact

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:52.320
would have been affected."

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:55.380
A court does not presume
that the outcome of a trial

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:56.550
would have been different

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:59.580
just because the lawyer's
performance was deficient,

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:02.370
and that is what doomed Syed's appeal.

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:04.680
The court said that even
if McClain's statements

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:07.290
about seeing Syed in the library was true,

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:10.560
her alibi does little more
that call into question

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:13.830
the time that the state
claimed Miss Lee was killed

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.840
and does nothing to rebut the evidence

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:19.080
establishing Mr. Syed's
motive and opportunity

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:20.460
to kill Miss Lee.

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.980
Thus, the jury could have disbelieved

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:26.460
that Mr. Syed killed Miss Lee by 2:36 p.m.

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:28.350
as the state's timeline suggested,

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:30.630
yet still believed that Mr. Syed

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:32.730
had the opportunity to kill Miss Lee

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.260
after 2:40 p.m.

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:36.840
Miss McClain's testimony
according to her affidavit

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:39.540
failed to account for
Mr. Syed's whereabouts

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:41.040
after 2:40 p.m.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:43.650
on January 13th, 1999.

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:46.560
Likewise, Mr. Syed's
statements to the police

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:48.630
failed to account for his whereabouts

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:51.660
after 2:15 p.m. when school let out.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:54.450
Therefore, even if the alibi testimony

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:56.550
had been admitted into evidence,

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:59.400
it could not have affected
the outcome of the case

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.530
because that evidence did not negate

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.990
Mr. Syed's criminal agency.

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:05.790
So although the court agreed

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:08.070
that Gutierrez's
representation was deficient

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.950
because she had failed to
investigate an alibi witness,

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:14.040
the majority concluded that
Syed was not prejudiced

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.810
by Gutierrez's mistakes.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:18.480
The court found that the
jury would have convicted him

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.270
based on Wilds' testimony
and the cell tower records.

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:24.750
As a result, Syed did not get a new trial.

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:26.850
But that's not the end of the story.

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:29.340
Syed's claims were given new life in 2020

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:32.700
after a new Maryland law gave
prosecutors the discretion

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:35.040
to modify the sentences of offenders

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.650
who were under 18 at
the time of their crimes

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:40.140
if they had served at
least 20 years in prison.

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:43.770
In 2021, Baltimore prosecutors
conducted an investigation

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:45.870
into the circumstances
of Syed's conviction

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:48.030
with the help of Syed's lawyers.

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:49.680
In March of 2022,

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.830
Baltimore prosecutors
agreed to new DNA testing,

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:54.990
saying that it was merited
because of advances

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:56.400
in genetic science.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.890
The prosecutor agreed
to the defense's request

00:13:58.890 --> 00:14:00.540
for touch DNA testing,

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:03.508
which was not available at
the time of Syed's trial.

00:14:03.508 --> 00:14:06.360
In September, prosecutors filed a motion

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.340
to vacate Syed's conviction.

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:11.190
Mosby accused the State
Attorney General's Office

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:12.750
of Brady violations.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:15.570
Now the Brady Rule requires prosecutors

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:18.510
to disclose materially
exculpatory evidence

00:14:18.510 --> 00:14:19.740
in the government's possession

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:20.790
to the defense.

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.830
Basically, this means that the prosecution

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:25.440
has to tell the defendant
about any evidence

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:27.810
that would potentially
negate a defendant's guilt,

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:30.180
that would reduce a
defendant's potential sentence,

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:33.300
or evidence going to the
credibility of the witness.

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:34.590
The prosecutors' motion

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:37.080
said that prosecutors
on the case decades ago

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.970
knew that there was another suspect

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:40.110
who threatened to kill Lee

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:42.360
and neglected to disclose that information

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:43.650
to defense attorneys.

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:47.280
Mosby asked that Syed be
granted a new trial at a minimum

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.770
and released on his own
personal recognizance.

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:52.530
A local judge agreed and Syed was freed.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:55.920
Mosby's office then had 30
days to complete its review.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:58.110
Maryland Attorney General Brian Frosh

00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:01.177
released a statement
disputing Mosby's allegations.

00:15:01.177 --> 00:15:04.170
"Among the other serious problems
with the motion to vacate,

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:07.770
the allegations related to
Brady violations are incorrect.

00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:11.190
Neither State's Attorney Mosby
nor anyone from her office

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:12.300
bothered to consult

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.130
with either the Assistant State's Attorney

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.450
who prosecuted the case

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:17.160
or with anyone in my office

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:19.320
regarding those alleged violations.

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:21.420
The file in this case was made available

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:23.910
on several occasions to the defense."

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:25.710
The friction between Mosby and Frosh

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:26.820
brings up another point.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:29.520
Why would Mosby exonerate Syed now?

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:32.340
The Maryland Supreme
Court denied Syed's appeal

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:35.250
and the US Supreme Court
refused to hear the case.

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:37.315
That would have finalized his conviction.

00:15:37.315 --> 00:15:38.610
(gavel thudding)

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:41.220
Activists on both sides of the Syed case

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:44.010
think that the decision
was politically motivated.

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:47.070
Here's DeRay Mckesson who
championed Syed's innocence

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:49.800
pointing out that Mosby
has some credibility issues

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:50.633
of her own.

00:15:50.633 --> 00:15:51.540
"See, here's the thing.

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:56.130
Mosby had the new DNA evidence
a la Adnan for a while now.

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:58.050
She didn't just get it yesterday.

00:15:58.050 --> 00:15:59.505
Why was the announcement yesterday?

00:15:59.505 --> 00:16:02.550
She waited to announce
to drown out coverage

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:04.140
of her own indictment."

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:06.420
And here's a blog post from
The Manhattan Institute

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:09.330
which argues against the
reforms Mosby tried to enact

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:12.037
and blames her for the city's
skyrocketing murder rate.

00:16:12.037 --> 00:16:14.700
"With the city reeling and
her reputation in tatters,

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:17.130
the safest exit strategy for Mosby

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:19.320
would have been to wind
down her role quietly,

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:20.580
hoping that nobody noticed

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:23.250
as she skulked off to
face her federal charges.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.620
Instead, Mosby is reinforcing

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:27.360
her de-prosecution credentials,

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:30.240
executing on a plan to free Adnan Syed,

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:32.306
convicted of killing a teenage girl."

00:16:32.306 --> 00:16:35.070
Their point? Well, Marilyn Mosby

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:38.520
was a lame duck.
- You're despicable.

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:40.230
- She was one of the first prosecutors

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:42.477
elected on a platform of decarceration.

00:16:42.477 --> 00:16:44.610
And that was in 2014.

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:48.480
In 2022, Baltimoreans
did not reelect Mosby.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.370
The Federal Government indicted Mosby

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:51.720
on two counts of perjury

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.580
and two counts of making false statements

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:54.900
on a loan application.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:57.000
The perjury counts involve Mosby

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:00.540
allegedly falsely claiming
a Covid-19 hardship

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:03.060
on applications to withdraw $90,000

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:04.530
from her retirement account.

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:06.150
The tax-free withdrawal option

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:08.640
was one of the benefits of the CARES Act.

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:11.310
Now the prosecutors'
investigation is complete.

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:13.380
Mosby looked at three main issues.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:16.650
DNA, alternate suspects,
and cellphone evidence.

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:19.080
Mosby said her office received DNA testing

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:22.590
on Lee's skirt, nylons, jacket, and shoes.

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:26.280
- Those items include skirt, pantyhose,

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:28.290
shoes and jacket

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:30.870
of Miss Hae Min Lee.

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:33.060
- [Devin] Forensic
scientists could not recover

00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:34.770
any DNA from the first three,

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:38.370
but they did find a DNA mixture
of multiple contributors

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:39.630
on Lee's shoes.

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:41.820
Mosby said, "Most compellingly,

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:44.637
Adnan Syed's DNA was excluded."

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.430
- And most compellingly,

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:51.840
Adnan Syed, his DNA was excluded.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:53.310
- Trace level male DNA

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:55.980
was detected on Lee's
right fingernail swabs,

00:17:55.980 --> 00:17:57.870
the right fingernail clipper swabs,

00:17:57.870 --> 00:17:59.550
and the victim's shirt swabs.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.100
The swabs from the right
fingernail and shirt

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.120
were then analyzed,

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:05.250
but no useful typing results were obtained

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:06.510
from this analysis.

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:07.620
Another shirt swab

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:10.710
and the right hand fingernail
clippings were not analyzed

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:13.320
because it was determined
that the amount of male DNA

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:14.490
was so minimal

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:17.100
it would not likely produce any results.

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:20.370
With respect to Brady material
on alternate suspects,

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:22.087
the Prosecutor's Office said they found

00:18:22.087 --> 00:18:24.900
"a separate document from
the original trial file

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:27.630
in which a different
person relaid information

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:30.720
that can be viewed as a
motive for the same suspect

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:31.920
to harm the victim.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:34.620
This information about the
threat and motives to harm

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:37.170
could have provided a
basis for the defense

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:39.330
and was not disclosed to the trial

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:41.910
nor the post-conviction defense counsel."

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:45.120
Mosby said that new
information also revealed

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:46.260
that one of the suspects

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:48.810
was convicted of attacking
a woman in her vehicle

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.730
and that one of the suspects was convicted

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.490
of engaging in serial
rape and sexual assault.

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:54.720
The investigators found out

00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:57.120
that Lee's car was located
right behind the house

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:59.670
of one of this suspect's family members.

00:18:59.670 --> 00:19:02.880
Some of this information was
available at the time of trial,

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:05.010
some of the events
occurred after the trial,

00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:06.540
according to the news release.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.280
As for the cellphone tower data,

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:11.490
the prosecutors found that
"based on the cellular technology

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:13.710
at the time of the incident in this case,

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:16.200
it was possible that an incoming call

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:19.590
could be recorded at the
last registered tower sector

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:20.790
and not the current one

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:23.250
when the signal was sent
across multiple towers

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:24.390
within an area."

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:27.210
The investigative team
said that two other experts

00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:28.470
verified this conclusion.

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:30.240
Mosby said that the investigation

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:31.710
into Lee's murder continues,

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:34.050
but she declined to offer any details.

00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:36.150
Presumably, the investigators will look

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:37.470
at the possible involvement

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:40.380
of two alternative
suspects other than Syed.

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:42.990
We don't know if the suspects
are involved individually

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:44.340
or involved together.

00:19:44.340 --> 00:19:45.810
According to the trial file,

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:47.317
one of these suspects said,

00:19:47.317 --> 00:19:50.010
"He would make her disappear,
he would kill her,"

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:51.600
referring to Miss Lee.

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:53.550
Mosby characterized Syed's conviction

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:55.650
as a miscarriage of justice.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:57.870
- As the administrator of
the criminal justice system,

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:00.270
it's my duty to ensure

00:20:00.270 --> 00:20:02.190
that justice is not delayed,

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:04.170
justice is never denied,

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:05.940
but justice be done.

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:09.030
- Lee's family does not
agree that justice was done.

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:10.170
They've expressed concerns

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:12.690
about why the Baltimore
County Prosecutor's Office

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:14.700
abruptly exonerated Syed

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:17.250
after insisting on his guilt for decades.

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:18.570
- They're very said.

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:20.040
I think they feel very hopeless

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:23.730
about any future justice being brought.

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:25.620
- The family also felt excluded

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:27.300
from the prosecutors' decision-making,

00:20:27.300 --> 00:20:29.130
stating that they were not informed

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:31.080
about the progress of the investigation.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:32.190
On September 29th,

00:20:32.190 --> 00:20:35.490
Lee's family filed a motion
opposing Syed's release,

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:38.040
asking a court to halt
the legal proceedings

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:39.930
to address alleged violations

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:42.150
of a state victim's rights law.

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:45.060
Lee's family says that
prosecutors didn't let them know

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:47.490
that they intended to
vacate Syed's sentence.

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:48.323
The motion says

00:20:48.323 --> 00:20:51.570
that two days after prosecutors
filed the motion to vacate

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:53.310
there was a meeting between prosecutors

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:54.720
and Syed's attorneys.

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:57.420
The family says they were not
notified of the proceeding

00:20:57.420 --> 00:21:00.390
and were later informed an
in-person hearing was scheduled

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:01.710
for the next business day,

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:05.610
leaving them with no opportunity
to attend or be heard.

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:07.470
Young Lee, who is Hae's brother,

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:10.200
filed a motion on the same
day as the September hearing,

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.360
stating he didn't have
enough notice to attend.

00:21:12.360 --> 00:21:14.760
The court went into recess
for about 30 minutes

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:16.590
while a call was hastily arranged

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:18.720
for Young Lee to express his confusion.

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:20.820
The court hasn't ruled
on the family's motion,

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:23.550
but it's unlikely to change the outcome.

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:25.507
Lee's family put out a statement, saying,

00:21:25.507 --> 00:21:29.070
"All this family ever wanted
was answers and a voice.

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:31.560
Today's actions robbed them of both."

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:34.080
And now let me burst
the true crime bubble.

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:36.150
Lee's family believes in Syed's guilt

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:37.710
and they have good reasons to.

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:40.260
There is a glaring hole
in the defense argument

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:43.560
that McClain provided Syed
with a rock-solid alibi.

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:45.120
In his accounts of where he went

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:46.440
on the day Lee was killed,

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:49.800
Syed never said that he was at
the Woodlawn Public Library.

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:52.500
McClain's testimony conflicted
with Syed's accounts

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:54.120
of his whereabouts that day,

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:57.960
which of course made Gutierrez's
client look untruthful.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:00.960
Gutierrez got into trouble
with the bar on other matters,

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:03.210
but that doesn't mean that she was wrong

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:04.890
not to reach out to McClain.

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:05.820
There's another problem

00:22:05.820 --> 00:22:08.370
with the Adnan was at the library alibi.

00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:10.380
It doesn't account for his whereabouts

00:22:10.380 --> 00:22:12.600
after about 2:40 p.m.

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:14.910
The state always asserted
that Lee was killed

00:22:14.910 --> 00:22:17.850
between 2:15 p.m. and 2:45 p.m.,

00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:19.440
but they don't know for sure.

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:22.890
Syed still had time to leave
the library, strangle Lee,

00:22:22.890 --> 00:22:24.480
get Wilds' help with the body,

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:27.450
and then head back to track
practice by early evening.

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:29.730
There's yet another angle
to the McClain story.

00:22:29.730 --> 00:22:31.650
How do we know she's telling the truth?

00:22:31.650 --> 00:22:33.000
The Attorney General's Office

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:34.926
said that two of McClain's classmates

00:22:34.926 --> 00:22:39.060
contacted them with allegations
that she made the story up.

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:40.770
The witnesses, who are sisters,

00:22:40.770 --> 00:22:42.930
remember talking with McClain about it

00:22:42.930 --> 00:22:44.340
in their co-op class,

00:22:44.340 --> 00:22:45.217
and I quote,

00:22:45.217 --> 00:22:48.360
"Both my sister and I, more so my sister,

00:22:48.360 --> 00:22:51.870
argued with Asia about how
serious this situation was.

00:22:51.870 --> 00:22:54.000
She just said that it
wouldn't hurt anything,

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:55.289
that if he was truly guilty,

00:22:55.289 --> 00:22:57.060
then he would be convicted.

00:22:57.060 --> 00:22:59.190
I'm not sure what can
come of this information,

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:01.770
but I felt I had to let someone know."

00:23:01.770 --> 00:23:04.080
Lots of people will say
that these two classmates

00:23:04.080 --> 00:23:05.340
who remain anonymous

00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:06.773
must be the liars.

00:23:06.773 --> 00:23:08.730
But that's the problem.

00:23:08.730 --> 00:23:12.300
People tend to draw inferences
about who's telling the truth

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:14.460
based on which side they're rooting for.

00:23:14.460 --> 00:23:16.470
McClain apparently wasn't so sure

00:23:16.470 --> 00:23:19.290
that her alibi meant Syed was innocent.

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:20.880
It seems even McClain knew

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:23.190
that if she saw Syed in the library,

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:26.640
it did not mean he wouldn't
have had time to kill Lee.

00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:29.587
She wrote to him when he
first went to prison, saying,

00:23:29.587 --> 00:23:32.430
"If you are innocent, I
will do my best to help you.

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:35.100
But if you're not, only God can help you."

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:36.757
McClain later published a book called

00:23:36.757 --> 00:23:39.720
"Confessions of a Serial Alibi."

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:41.490
The Attorney General's Office pushed back

00:23:41.490 --> 00:23:42.810
against Mosby's claim

00:23:42.810 --> 00:23:45.607
that the McClain information
was withheld from the defense.

00:23:45.607 --> 00:23:48.600
"Among the other serious problems
with the motion to vacate,

00:23:48.600 --> 00:23:52.110
the allegations related to
Brady violations are incorrect."

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:55.177
The office said in a news
release issued after the hearing,

00:23:55.177 --> 00:23:56.760
"Neither State's Attorney Mosby

00:23:56.760 --> 00:23:58.350
nor anyone else from her office

00:23:58.350 --> 00:23:59.220
bothered to consult

00:23:59.220 --> 00:24:01.110
with either the Assistant State's Attorney

00:24:01.110 --> 00:24:02.370
who prosecuted the case

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:03.780
or with anyone in my office

00:24:03.780 --> 00:24:05.700
regarding these alleged violations.

00:24:05.700 --> 00:24:06.960
The file in this case

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:09.420
was made available on several occasions

00:24:09.420 --> 00:24:10.620
to the defense."

00:24:10.620 --> 00:24:12.270
Moreover, it's worth pointing out

00:24:12.270 --> 00:24:14.640
that the inconsistencies
in Wilds' accounts

00:24:14.640 --> 00:24:15.900
of what happened that day

00:24:15.900 --> 00:24:17.700
were actually addressed head on

00:24:17.700 --> 00:24:20.040
by the prosecution during trial.

00:24:20.040 --> 00:24:21.990
And then there's the
new touch DNA evidence.

00:24:21.990 --> 00:24:24.720
It revealed that there were
multiple DNA contributors

00:24:24.720 --> 00:24:25.830
on Lee's shoe,

00:24:25.830 --> 00:24:27.720
but none of them Syed.

00:24:27.720 --> 00:24:28.980
So what does that mean?

00:24:28.980 --> 00:24:31.748
Well, honestly, not a lot.

00:24:31.748 --> 00:24:34.200
It could mean Syed never touched the shoe,

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:36.300
or it could mean Syed did touch the shoe

00:24:36.300 --> 00:24:38.127
but not enough or in the right way

00:24:38.127 --> 00:24:40.620
to transfer his DNA onto it.

00:24:40.620 --> 00:24:44.730
By itself, it really doesn't mean much.

00:24:44.730 --> 00:24:47.250
So although Adnan Syed has been exonerated

00:24:47.250 --> 00:24:48.390
by the State of Maryland,

00:24:48.390 --> 00:24:49.890
the question remains.

00:24:49.890 --> 00:24:51.570
Who killed Hae Min Lee

00:24:51.570 --> 00:24:53.790
back in January of 1999?

00:24:53.790 --> 00:24:54.990
Was it one suspect

00:24:54.990 --> 00:24:56.910
or two people working in concert?

00:24:56.910 --> 00:24:58.530
Did investigators know their names

00:24:58.530 --> 00:25:00.660
during Syed's trial in 2000?

00:25:00.660 --> 00:25:03.060
Sources say that Baltimore
County prosecutors

00:25:03.060 --> 00:25:05.760
are mostly considering old suspects.

00:25:05.760 --> 00:25:08.040
Of course, there was presumably a reason

00:25:08.040 --> 00:25:10.975
that these suspects weren't
pursued in the original case.

00:25:10.975 --> 00:25:12.510
What were those reasons?

00:25:12.510 --> 00:25:14.670
And what did the Maryland
Attorney General's Office

00:25:14.670 --> 00:25:15.840
know about them?

00:25:15.840 --> 00:25:17.970
And perhaps, most importantly,

00:25:17.970 --> 00:25:21.240
is Mosby able to test those suspects' DNA?

00:25:21.240 --> 00:25:22.350
Only time will tell,

00:25:22.350 --> 00:25:24.903
but Syed will be spending
that time a free man.

